            <ArticleTitle>Angiographically documented thrombotic coronary artery occlusion secondary to mild nonpenetrating thoracic trauma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>179-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 22-yr-old man was found to have a subtotally occluding thrombus in the proximal left anterior descending (LAD) coronary artery shortly after suffering mild blunt chest trauma. After 6 days of anticoagulant therapy, the LAD appeared angiographically normal.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
